findings.body:
`let waiter = XCTWaiter.wait(for: [expect], timeout: timeout)` assigns a value that is never read. The result of the wait is also discarded, so a timeout is indistinguishable from a delegate that ran without a frame. The bare `return` at the end of `decidePolicyFor` is also redundant. The `guard let (frame, origin) = ...` block is copied three times in the test file, so it could be a single helper or a shared setup.

::code{file="BrowserKit/Tests/WebEngineTests/Utilities/WebKitTestHelpers.swift" lines="44-48"}

If you keep the helper, drop the unused binding and return `nil` early on timeout, or call `XCTFail` with the wait result so the failure message says whether the navigation timed out.
